-# System architecture
+# LoopRank system architecture
 
-This is a recommendation-ranking system. Its input is structured user, video
-and impression context; its output is a click score and descending candidate
-rank. It does not analyze media authenticity.
+LoopRank is an autonomous research and ranking system for the Starter Kit's
+KuaiRand `long_view` task. It consumes structured user/video impression rows
+and emits one ranking score per test row. It does not analyze video pixels,
+audio, factual claims, or authenticity.
 
 ![Input and output scope](assets/system-scope.svg)
 
 ```mermaid
 flowchart LR
-    A[Official KuaiRand-Pure archive] --> B[MD5 verification and safe extraction]
-    B --> C[Fixed train / validation / quarantined test split]
-    C --> D[Leakage audit and manifest]
-    D --> E[Feature encoder fit on train only]
-    E --> F[MF / DeepFM / DCN / multi-task DCN]
-    O[Structured model-driven policy] -->|metrics + failures| G[Bounded research agent]
-    G -->|hypothesis + config diff| F
-    F --> H[A100 training]
-    H --> I[NDCG@10 + Recall@50]
-    I --> G
-    H --> J[Atomic validation-best checkpoint]
-    G --> K[Convergence / walltime / experiment budget]
-    G --> L[OOM, NaN and CUDA recovery]
-    G --> M[Iteration JSONL + resource report]
-    J --> N[Final selected model]
-    M --> N
-    N --> P[Label-blind ranked CSV + checksum]
+    A[Official KuaiRand data] --> B[Starter Kit date split]
+    B --> C[Train-only feature fitting]
+    C --> D[Bounded model candidates]
+    P[GPT-5 mini policy] -->|hypothesis + config diff| E[Research controller]
+    D --> E
+    E --> F[Train / recover]
+    F --> G[GAUC + nDCG at 5]
+    G -->|metrics + reflection| P
+    F --> H[Validation-best checkpoints]
+    E --> I[Iteration + token + recovery logs]
+    H --> J[Validation-only ensemble]
+    J --> K[Four-column test CSV]
+    K --> L[Schema + checksum verification]
 ```
 
-## Safety boundaries
+## Autonomous control contract
 
-- The development API accepts only train and validation paths; it has no test
-  argument.
-- Categorical vocabularies are fit exclusively on training rows. Unseen
-  validation categories map to a reserved unknown bucket.
-- Only logged non-click impressions are used as negatives. No external data or
-  synthetic unexposed pairs are introduced.
-- The cumulative video-statistics file is excluded because it may contain
-  future-derived aggregates.
-- Checkpoints are written atomically and selected by validation metrics.
+The OpenAI policy receives the bounded candidate set plus prior hypotheses,
+metrics, errors, and recoveries. It returns a strict-schema decision and
+reflection; it cannot execute arbitrary generated code. The controller trains
+that candidate, records the exact diff and outcome, applies bounded recovery
+rules when necessary, and stops on convergence or budget.
 
-## Autonomous control contract
+The official audit run completed six GPT-5 mini decisions with 5,971 measured
+API tokens and zero manual experiment interventions. Its best checkpoint is
+preserved even though the final validation-only ensemble scored higher.
+
+## Leakage and correctness boundaries
+
+- Features, categorical mappings, and history aggregates are fitted on
+  training data only.
+- Model and blend selection use validation only.
+- Prediction exporters read test identity/context columns but never test
+  outcomes.
+- Submission order is preserved exactly through a continuous zero-based
+  `row_id`.
+- Checkpoints are validation-best and the final ensemble recipe is explicit.
+- The required CSV is independently checked with the Starter Kit.
+
+## Evidence boundary
 
-Each candidate is a bounded hypothesis with a configuration diff. In
-model-driven mode, the policy reads previous metrics, errors, and recoveries and
-selects the next candidate through a strict JSON schema; offline mode provides
-a reproducible queue. The agent trains, evaluates, records the outcome, and
-either advances, retries safely, or stops on convergence/budget. It does not
-execute arbitrary generated code on the cluster. This makes the run
-reproducible, inexpensive, and auditable.
+`submission/03_run_iteration_logs/` contains the complete agent audit.
+`submission/04_final_submission_results/` contains outputs, checkpoints,
+results/deltas, resource usage, schema proof, and artifact hashes.
