+The winning ensemble improves the published primary baseline by **0.001991
+absolute**. Its blend uses 55% three-seed FM average, 12.5% DeepFM, and 32.5%
+three-seed context-FM average, selected on validation only. The final
+KuaiRand-Pure file contains 170,588 aligned rows and passes the independent
+Starter Kit checker.
+
+For the portal checklist, the same validation predictions score **0.812924
+NDCG@10 / 0.999979 Recall@50**. These are supplemental: the Starter Kit's
+executable protocol uses GAUC/nDCG@5. Recall@50 is nearly saturated on Pure
+because 99.9166% of evaluated users have no more than 50 candidates.
+
+The completed KuaiRand-1K A100 run reached **0.647500 GAUC / 0.571905
+nDCG@5 / 0.609702 primary**, plus supplemental **0.562493 NDCG@10 /
+0.096342 Recall@50**, and exported 4,132,081 aligned rows.
+
+The OpenAI-driven Pure research agent also completed **6/6 bounded
+experiments**, with all decisions made by `gpt-5-mini`, **5,971 measured API
+tokens**, and **0 manual interventions**. It stopped on convergence and selected
+the auxiliary-weight-0.1 multitask DCN at **0.668100 GAUC / 0.536646 nDCG@5 /
+0.602373 primary**. The stronger seed-averaged ensemble remained the final
+submission, while the agent checkpoint, rationales, reflections, and exact
+token audit are included as autonomy evidence.
+
+Total measured training/evaluation accelerator use was **0.765908 GPU-hours**,
+including the failed 19-second NSCC allocation. The OpenAI portion used **4,112
+input tokens and 1,859 output tokens**. Across the recorded research work there
+were 14 automated recovery events and no manual experiment interventions.
+
+## Challenges and recoveries
+
+The supplied repository initially followed a different click/NDCG@10/
+Recall@50 protocol. Reading the Starter Kit exposed the mismatch, so we
+quarantined those outputs and rebuilt evaluation and submission around
+long_view, GAUC, and nDCG@5.
+
+LambdaRank initially failed because SciPy was incomplete, then because source
+rows were not globally grouped by user. The agent repaired the dependency and
+stable-sorted only the training/evaluation views while preserving submission
+row order. The first large-scale evaluator made the same contiguity assumption;
+it was replaced with global official grouping before the integration smoke
+test. No human intervention was needed during the completed local run.
+
+The first OpenAI-mode NSCC launch also revealed that compute nodes reset
+outbound API connections. The agent recorded the failure, retained the strict
+OpenAI configuration, and completed the identical bounded run locally where
+API egress was available; no queued fallback was used.
 
 ## What we learned
 
-Simply forcing the last epoch was counterproductive. The final DCN had an
-80-epoch ceiling, stopped after 12, and restored epoch 2. Early stopping,
-regularization, learning-rate control, and faithful negative exposure were more
-valuable than raw epoch count.
-
-The challenge statement references CWM, but the public upstream CWM repository
-optimizes counterfactual watch-time/long-view objectives rather than the stated
-click + Recall@50 contract. We retained its DeepFM/DCN backbone families while
-making the click objective and evaluation assumptions explicit.
-
-## Challenges
-
-- The later official log is not globally timestamp-sorted, so literal row
-  halves overlap in time. The manifest records this rather than silently
-  changing organizer membership.
-- Logged-impression Recall@50 is close to one because many users have fewer than
-  50 logged candidates. Candidate-count diagnostics quantify the saturation; we
-  also report a much harder full-catalog popularity result and clearly flag the
-  missing organizer evaluator.
-- NSCC's current PyTorch modulefile points to `site-package` instead of
-  `site-packages`; the PBS job applies a narrow path correction and validates
-  imports in a scheduled bootstrap job.
-
-## Resource use
-
-- Hardware: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-40GB on NSCC ASPIRE2A.
-- Recorded primary GPU time: 0.56667 GPU-hours.
-- Recorded optional 1K training GPU time: 0.41944 PBS GPU-hours (export
-  inference reported separately).
-- Manual model-training interventions: 0; bonus integration interventions: 2
-  (one row-split audit correction and one export batch-size correction).
-- Successful GPT-5 mini policy decision: 1,513 input + 388 output tokens,
-  estimated $0.001154. One earlier capped request returned incomplete JSON;
-  combined API spend remained below $0.01.
-- Datasets: KuaiRand-Pure required benchmark plus the permitted KuaiRand-1K
-  bonus benchmark; no unrelated external training data.
-
-## Limitations and next steps
-
-The organizer evaluation script, official numeric baseline, convergence epsilon,
-and final submission schema were not included in the supplied materials. The
-pipeline isolates these interfaces so they can be replaced without rewriting
-training. The final repository includes a generic label-blind schema adapter,
-multi-feedback objectives, repeated-seed evaluation, and an optional
-KuaiRand-1K bonus pipeline.
